# Android services stubbed out on bramble (Pixel 4a 5G) because they only spam
# the journal under LuneOS/Halium (see meta-android's pre-start.d/50-stub-services).
#
# Same Pixel vendor stack as sargo and sunfish, so the same list, minus what
# device/google/redbull does not ship. Nothing here is confirmed against a
# running device; a path that does not exist is simply never stubbed.
#
# Pixel telemetry reporter; polls the never-present IStats framework service.
vendor/bin/pixelstats-vendor
# Titan M reboot-escrow HAL; polls keymaster hwservices that never register.
vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.rebootescrow-service.citadel
# Display post-processing daemon; needs the framework sensorservice for the
# ambient light sensor and crash-loops without it.
vendor/bin/mm-pp-dpps
# On-device modem/diag loggers. diag_mdlog holds DIAG_WS and the cdsp/lpass
# IPC-router ports awake - measured on sargo as the suspend aborter. init
# exec-starts it as a oneshot, so the stub must exit rather than sleep.
vendor/bin/diag_mdlog exit
vendor/bin/ssr_diag
# Android's storaged, which polls hwservicemanager once a second when the
# health HAL is absent. LuneOS's own storaged is a different daemon outside
# the container.
system/bin/storaged
